It is Wednesday afternoon.
Rohan and I come out of the office.
We have done a lot of work in the office in the morning.
So we want a short break now.
We go to the tea stall across the street.
The tea vendor is making hot tea.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, give us two cutting chais."
Rohan smiles and says, "And make it a bit strong!"
We take the tea glasses in our hands.
This hot tea feels very nice after the office's AC.
Rohan asks me, "Maya, have you roamed around a lot in Mumbai?"
I say, "Yes, I have learned to travel here."
"I travel by bus every day."
"And I have also traveled by metro."
Rohan drinks his tea and says, "Oh wow, that is very nice."
I smile and say, "Life here is fast, but I have liked it."
We finish our tea.
I give fifteen rupees to the tea vendor.
Now we have become ready for work again.
